# Production build settings. Committed on purpose.
#
# `VITE_API_URL` must be baked in at BUILD time -- Vite inlines
# import.meta.env.* into the bundle, so there is no runtime configuration to
# change afterwards. Without this, src/lib/api.js falls back to its
# http://localhost:4000 default and the deployed shop talks to a machine that
# only exists on a developer's laptop: the catalogue renders empty for every
# real visitor and isAdmin never arrives, so the admin panel stays hidden.
#
# This file exists rather than relying on netlify.toml's [build.environment]
# because that only applies when Netlify itself runs the build. A `build/`
# folder built locally and uploaded by hand never sees it -- which is exactly
# how the shop shipped pointing at localhost.
#
# Not a secret: the API hostname is public, and anything VITE_-prefixed is
# visible to every visitor anyway.
VITE_API_URL=https://timeless-baazar-api.onrender.com
